1405-07-30 10/22/2026 v10.0.13
- package update
1405-06-02 8/24/2026 v10.0.11.9
- (breaking) KamiSama.Templates is redesigned as 11 composable solution, project-family and item scaffolds. The public catalog is now kamisama-solution, kamisama-bc, kamisama-provider, kamisama-bootstrap, kamisama-server, kamisama-type, kamisama-crud, kamisama-feature, kamisama-panel-crud, kamisama-aspire-local and kamisama-delete-button.
- The retired kamisama-admin, kamisama-empty, kamisama-bounded-context, kamisama-database-support and kamisama-orchestration commands are removed rather than retained as incompatible aliases.
- kamisama-solution now creates an AI-ready .slnx shell with optional props.xml, modular YAML design files, agent/solution-map.yaml, updated AGENTS.md guidance and independently selectable snapshots of the KamiSama Libraries and KamiSama Solution Designer skills.
- The new kamisama-solution-designer skill adds a validated modular YAML design language for bounded contexts, providers, ordered Bootstrap initialization, external services, unified API/daemon/panel servers, hosted-service schedules, APIs, pages, hints and inferred orchestration.
- Project scaffolds enforce the <Solution>.<Context or Server>.<Role> naming convention, provider-neutral bounded contexts, provider-owned migrations, ordered Bootstrap initializers and unified server families with an optional Blazor WebAssembly client.
- Item scaffolds add public entities/data types, KamiSama FeatureDefinitionBase CRUD services, individual operations, panel List/Details/Save vertical slices, Aspire database/initialization environment helpers and a confirmed asynchronous Blazor Bootstrap DeleteButton.
- Generated OpenCode configuration discovers selected project skills, and the solution map records verified implemented topology while C# remains authoritative for behavior.
- Packed-template validation now verifies exactly 11 manifests, all skill combinations, props modes, all four EF Core providers, API and Blazor server modes, item placement and a composed solution containing bounded-context CRUD, panel CRUD and DeleteButton scaffolds.
- Template documentation, package metadata and generated onboarding are updated for the redesigned catalog and template-first design workflow.
1405-05-31 8/22/2026 v10.0.11.8
- KamiSama solution templates expose a Visual Studio Create solution directory option. It defaults to disabled so generated content is placed directly in the selected location, while users can enable it to create a solution-named directory.
- The solution-directory option is limited to kamisama-solution, kamisama-bounded-context, kamisama-orchestration and kamisama-admin; single-project templates retain their existing layout.
1405-05-30 8/21/2026 v10.0.11.7
- (breaking) The previous Props, Abstractions, Core, Database and Blazor Admin templates are replaced by kamisama-solution, kamisama-admin, kamisama-empty, kamisama-bounded-context, kamisama-database-support, kamisama-bootstrap and kamisama-orchestration.
- KamiSama AI Ready Solution generates an empty .slnx, optional props.xml, GETTING_STARTED.md, AGENTS.md and vendor-neutral .agents guidance without an architecture manifest.
- KamiSama Admin Panel generates canonical Abstractions and Core layers, a Blazor client, an authorized ASP.NET Core server and either a new or explicitly referenced shared Bootstrap project. User Management and Ticketing are supported independently.
- KamiSama Bounded Context and Orchestration generate infrastructure-independent Abstractions and provider-neutral Core projects with optional examples, public localization resources, WebModule registration and attribute-based dependency injection.
- KamiSama Database Support generates a separate PostgreSQL, SQLite, SQL Server or Oracle project for an explicitly selected bounded-context Core project.
- KamiSama Bootstrap provides a reusable composition root for multiple servers. Identity/User Management and Ticketing support independently selected PostgreSQL or SQLite providers, and Ticketing includes its hidden Identity dependency automatically.
- props.xml is optional across the templates; projects remain independently compilable when it is disabled, configurable imports are used when enabled, and provider/project suffix namespace handling is corrected.
- Template packaging now pins Microsoft.TemplateEngine.Tasks, includes a valid NuGet README and hidden .agents content, and avoids duplicate content/content package paths and obsolete large frontend assets.
- Packed-template validation now installs the local package, verifies the public template list, generates and builds the complete option/provider matrix, and removes the temporary template installation and generated output.
- Template documentation is rewritten for the new public templates, composition workflows, provider matrix, AI guidance, official Aspire tooling and Visual Studio limitations.
- KamiSama.Repositories.EntityFrameworkCore.SqlServer is added with SQL Server multi-provider DbContext registration.
- KamiSama.Repositories.EntityFrameworkCore.Oracle is added with Oracle multi-provider DbContext registration.
1405-05-28 8/19/2026 v10.0.11.6
- KamiSama.Modules.Otp.* are added.
- KamiSama.Modules.Contents.* are added.
- modules migrations are updated.
- KamiSama.Modules.Identity.Services.Authentication.ITokenService is added.
- packages updated.
1405-05-23 8/14/2026 v10.0.11.1
- KamiSama.Extensions.WebModules is renamed to KamiSama.Modules.
- KamiSama.ServicePlans Module is added.
- KamiSama.PolicyEngine Module is added.
- NuGet package descriptions are refined and obsolete package release notes are removed.
- Package API documentation is included as the NuGet README when available.
- (breaking) Identity authentication contracts are moved from Services.Users to Services.Authentication and replaced by ILogin, IRefreshToken, ILogout, and ILogoutAll.
- Identity login now accepts one user name or email value and returns the authenticated user with revocable session tokens and the access-token expiration.
- Low-level Identity token issuance is internalized, current-session and all-session logout are added, and the Identity API documentation, descriptions, and examples are updated.
- API documentation for all 52 packages is reviewed and expanded with package-specific installation, setup, usage, examples, and verified runtime and publication caveats.
- Public and protected API XML documentation, NuGet package descriptions, and generated namespace, type, and member guidance are completed across the library families.
- The API documentation generator now reads the canonical root version, excludes non-public APIs, and preserves per-package review snapshots and approved example exemptions during regeneration.
- The complete generated documentation is regenerated and validated with a strict MkDocs build.
- Ticketing now validates status transitions: open or reopened tickets can be resolved, resolved tickets can be reopened or closed, closed tickets are terminal, and invalid transitions return an HTTP 409 conflict. Ticketing documentation, examples, and transition tests are updated accordingly.
